
■ Local database already has application tables but no Void migration history.

  Existing tables: accounts, admins, artisan_regions, audit_log, 
  auth_credentials, auth_sessions, auth_users, auth_verifications, chargebacks, 
  completions, conversations, d1_migrations, data_requests, disputes, 
  due_clocks, engagements, fake_payment_state, invitations, job_edits, 
  job_matches, jobs, ledger_entries, marketplace_rules, messages, names_sent, 
  notices, payments, payout_runs, payouts, profile_edits, queue_items, 
  quote_revisions, quotes, rate_limit_hits, refunds, refused_sends, regions, 
  reports, reviews, sightings, signals, suburbs, support_requests, suspensions, 
  updated_quotes, verification_checks, warnings

  This usually means the schema was applied with `void db push` or the local 
  database was created before migration tracking existed.
  Run `void db reset` to recreate the local database from db/migrations/, or 
  delete the local D1 state if you do not need its data.
